Z||000002||StuGood||10-29-2000||01:12 PM||||All right, batboy, are you getting commissions from Pontiac, for bragging up their Grand Prix's?  I'm calling the spam police !!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  J/K - I know how it is, when you find a car you actually <B>like</B>.  Hope it gives you many miles /years of good service and fun driving.<P>BTW, I've <B>seen</B> that giant Coor's silo, but I forget where it is-?  <P>   <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000003||batboy||10-29-2000||05:41 PM||||The giant Coors can is near the Emporia Turnpike tollbooths. Hey, I had to get rid of one Fiero to make room for the GP, but I'm still going to be a two Fiero family. I'm keeping the Batmobile, no doubt.<P>Seriously Stetz, there are several affordable late 80's and early 90's quick cars. What about the Buick Grand Nationals and the 89-90 turbo Grand Prixes? Lots of GM cars that had performance packages with the TDC 3.4 or the Quad 4 engines. I saw several older, inexpensive, supercharged Bonnevilles for sale. You can cruise in comfort with a whole bunch of friends in one of those bad boys.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-29-2000||06:21 PM||||Most of the Grand Nationals I've seen (in good shape) haven't been all that affordable, especially the GNX variation (faster than poop through a duck, whatever that means).  A friend of mine has one of the GTP Grand Prixs.  Previous body style, wing, body armor, etc.  Nice car, rode well, good on gas, and hold-on-to-your-butt-both-feet-flat-on-the-floor-my-moms-gonna-kill-me-if-we-get-caught-at-this-speed, etc.  He paid somewhere around $8000 a couple of years ago.||||reg||1
Z||000005||olympic||10-29-2000||06:25 PM||||  I've seen a website where a guy tried to swap a 3.4 TDC into a ~90 Cavalier.  He said the engine(mainly the heads) was way too big to fit under the hood.  So he ended up putting a turbo on his 3.1.  I would imagine that a Beretta wouldn't have any more under-hood room than a Cavalier.<P>  The 3.8 is a 90 degree V6 so it would also be way wider than a 2.8.<P>  I'm a real fan of strange engine swaps though!  My current project is to swap a <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/shomotor.gif">  <P>into my '94<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right16.jpg">  <P>   <BR>  A few mods will put this engine at 200 hp @ the wheels.   Combine that with a Quaife LSD and it'll be a real stang/f-bod eater.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Can't wait till I take her to the track and see the jaws drop when a 19 second econo-box rips a mid 14 second pass!!...lol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by olympic (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
